      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "upon reading this\n\nI was able to just go to the *blenshape normals* drop down and select none\n\nThere is a update issue with vrchat SDK where it wont update anything in the stats viewer.   So I hide the avatars container game object.    switch back to vrchat sdk and then the avatar vanishes and the sdk says no avatar detected\n\nI then unhide the avatar and sdk sees avatars and updates\n\nSo i was able to get the warning away by just setting blenshape normal to none.\n\nI would like to have blenshape normal in a limited amount\n\nI have dragon arm mesh that I transform into. Id love to shape key a shirt sleeve that changes to fit the added arm.   without the normal being messed up.    but without controlling content when making games unlike vrchat\n\nThe download size would skyrocket :(\n\none could argue that i just have another shirt that fits the new arm but then? blenshape normals would be LESS size, then a whole new shirt maybe? i dont know the data about blendshape normals I wish i did",
